# Multilingual + spec packs ship with the installer (tier 1)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-16):

> **Confirm that all spec packages ship with the installer and are part of
> common assets including multilingual assets. Multilingual assets for all
> components are shipped with the installer. Multilingual support is a
> tier 1 supported capability.**

## The rule

> **Multilingual support is tier 1 — not an optional add-on and not a
> later wave. Every spec package (CMMC, NIST 800-171 / 172 / 53, PCI,
> GDPR, California, Spec 24 / Spec 2400, Spec 42 catalog, and any future
> spec) and every language catalog the product ships must live in
> `core-assets/content/` and must be present in the product installer
> (on disk and/or compiled into a shipping EXE). Omitting a spec pack or
> a language from the MSI is a defect.**

## Common-assets home

| Tree | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `core-assets/content/auditor-playbooks/` | Every playbook JSON (including `scaffold-spec-24.json`) |
| `core-assets/content/locales/<tag>/` | Server catalogs (binder, reports, risks, cli, messaging, disclosures). **Shipped today:** `en`, `de`, `es`, `fr`. **Tier 1 also requires** `en-GB` and `zh-Hans` — see language tiers. |
| `core-assets/content/locales-ui/<tag>/` | Admin-SPA locale JSON (inspectable MSI copy) |
| `core-assets/content/i18n-native/` | Native GUI / agent / recording catalogs (`pim-app-config-i18n` bundles) |

`scripts/sync-to-projects.ps1` mirrors playbooks and server locales into
`pim-offline-server`. Native bundles sync into `pim-app-config-i18n`.

Branding and legal stay under [`branding-assets.mdc`](branding-assets.mdc).
This rule covers **content packs**, not icons or EULAs.

## How each surface ships

| Surface | In the EXE | On disk in the MSI |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Control catalog (CMMC, NIST, Spec 42, Spec 24, …) | Yes — `pim-compliance-catalog` | Playbook JSON under `auditor-playbooks\` |
| Training / welcome templates | Yes — `training/templates*.rs` | Locale JSON when a catalog exists |
| Auditor playbooks | Seeded from install-tree JSON | **Required** — every `*.json` except `_` scratch |
| Server locales (every shipped tag) | Yes — `include_str` | **Required** — `INSTALLFOLDER\locales\` |
| Admin SPA locales | Yes — Vite bundle | **Required** — `INSTALLFOLDER\locales\ui\` |
| Native operator GUIs, agent, recording | Yes — `pim-app-config-i18n` `include_str` | Canonical copies in `core-assets/content/i18n-native/` |

A catalog that exists only in a repo and is not in `core-assets/content/`
**or** not in the MSI / shipping EXE has not shipped.

## Required agent behavior

1. **New spec pack** — add the playbook (or document catalog-only + why),
   add EN and at least DE locale strings in the same change set, copy
   into `core-assets/content/`, add the WiX `File` + MSI required-list
   row, and extend `sync-to-projects.ps1` if a new tree is needed.
2. **New language** — add `locales/<tag>/` catalogs, register in
   `i18n_content.rs` / `pim-app-config-i18n`, stage in the MSI, copy to
   `core-assets/content/`. A data add, not a code rewrite. Tier 1 tags
   (`en`, `en-GB`, `de`, `fr`, `es`, `zh-Hans`) are mandatory for
   compliance documentation; missing tags are **BLOCKED**, not optional.
3. **Do not** treat lab `Deploy-OfflineServerDev.ps1` copy as installer
   proof. The MSI required list and `installer.wxs` must name the file.
4. Mirror this rule to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` in the same change
   set ([`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc)).

## Forbidden

- Shipping a spec (Spec 24, PCI, …) in git / lab deploy but omitting it
  from `Build-PimOfflineServerMsi.ps1` `$requiredPlaybooks` or WiX.
- English-only installer trees when DE (or another shipped tag) catalogs
  exist in the repo.
- Calling multilingual “nice to have,” “phase 2,” or “optional SKU.”
- Inventing a product env var for locale
  ([`no-environment-variables.mdc`](no-environment-variables.mdc)).

## Must-localize compliance artifacts

Reports, evidence exports, policy docs, risk templates, regulatory
mappings, legal/privacy/DPA/consent text, session-recording and access
evidence, change logs, IR documentation, and compliance dashboards are
**must-localize**. See
[`compliance-artifacts-must-localize.mdc`](compliance-artifacts-must-localize.mdc)
(artifact list **and** language tiers). English-only shipping text on
those surfaces is a defect even when the MSI already copies a locale
folder. Tier 1 is incomplete until `en-GB` and `zh-Hans` catalogs ship.

